s in Box\n17,Savings Box,Savings Take Out in Box,Total Savings in Box\n18,Product,Price,Ammount\n","align":0,"rect":[0,0,324,208],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1055":{"name":"CurrentPage","type":"text","text":"3","align":0,"rect":[0,0,24,23],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":21,"ascent":15,"style":0,"size":18,"color":"#fcd5af","font":"Arial"}]},"1056":{"name":"Name1","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,200,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":null}]},"1057":{"name":"Name2","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,207,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":null}]},"1058":{"name":"PicText","type":"text","text":"1879\n1880\n1881\n1882\n1887\n1888\n1890\n1891\n1893\n1894\n1909\n1910\n1914\n1915\n1917\n1919\n","align":0,"rect":[0,0,324,272],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1059":{"name":"InOut","type":"text","text":"5","align":0,"rect":[0,0,89,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1060":{"name":"In","type":"text","text":"You have $904 in cash.  How much money do you want to put into your box?","align":0,"rect":[0,0,217,54],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":18,"ascent":14,"style":0,"size":14,"color":"#000000","font":"Times New Roman"}]},"1061":{"name":"Out","type":"text","text":"How much money do you want to take out of the box?","align":0,"rect":[0,0,189,36],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":18,"ascent":14,"style":0,"size":14,"color":"#000000","font":"Times New Roman"}]},"1062":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"You don't have enough money \n            to do this.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,231,36],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":18,"ascent":14,"style":0,"size":14,"color":"#000000","font":"Times New Roman"}]},"1063":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Amount of savings","align":0,"rect":[0,0,143,22],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":22,"ascent":17,"style":0,"size":18,"color":"#000000","font":"Times New Roman"}]},"1064":{"name":"MySavings","type":"text","text":"","align":1,"rect":[0,0,88,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":null}]},"1299":{"name":"AT","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,251,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":null}]},"1301":{"name":"T1","type":"text","text":"March, 1880\nWe're ready to say good-bye to city life on the East Coast.  We'll travel first by train and then by covered wagon to the High Plains of Kansas. Once we're there, we'll stake a claim for a homestead of 160 acres. Our family is ready to go west and make a new start!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,567,64],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1302":{"name":"T2","type":"text","text":"April, 1880\nWe've finally made it to Kansas!  We've found a  good spot for our homestead, not far from a creek  and a small town.  Until we build a house, we're  living in a tent made from the top of our covered wagon.  Once we get settled, we'll get ready to farm our homestead.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,425,80],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1303":{"name":"ATexts","type":"text","text":"We're so proud of our youngest daughter.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,419,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1304":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We're so proud of our eldest son.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,200,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1305":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Our neighbors helped us build this sod house in just one day!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,441,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1306":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We finally covered our sod walls with wooden planks. Now it feels like a real house.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,433,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1307":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Things have been going very well on the homestead.  Now we live in this new house instead of our old one.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,424,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1308":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We've been living on the homestead for five years now. According to the Homestead Act, now the land is really ours!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,431,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1309":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Before we built our well, we had to carry pails of water from the creek every day.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,453,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1310":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Our team of horses sure have a good appetite at the end of a day's work in the fields.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,438,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1311":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Some folks use oxen instead of horses to pull their hay wagon.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,410,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1312":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We finally had enough money to buy some furniture from the store.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,411,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1313":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Farming is much easier with a big  steam-engine tractor.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,442,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1314":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"The general store sells just about anything you'd want to buy.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,495,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1315":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Plowing this hard, dry soil is not easy.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,390,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1316":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Our windmill pumps water from deep underground.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,439,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1317":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"Out here, a town can be built in just a day or two.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,432,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1318":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We're just starting out, so we made nearly  everything we own with our own hands.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,480,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1319":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"There's nothing as exciting as watching the 12:05 roar into town.  Who knows which letters, packages, or visitors will be on board?","align":0,"rect":[0,0,443,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1320":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"There's plenty of open space on the Great Plains for farmers, cowboys, and their herds of cattle.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,560,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1321":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"This winter there's plenty of hay for our horses and cows.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,387,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1322":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"This year, three generations of our family sat down to a big Thanks giving dinner.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,444,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1323":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"We miss our eldest daughter, who lives with her husband in Detroit.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,400,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1324":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"This year, our first son was born!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,200,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1325":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"This year, our second son was born!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,200,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1326":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"This year, our second daughter was born!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,345,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1327":{"name":"ATextsE","type":"text","text":"We're so proud of our younger son.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,200,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1328":{"name":"T18834","type":"text","text":"The Brooklyn Bridge in New York City is finally ready. If our creek were as wide as New York's East River, we'd have all the water we need.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,577,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1329":{"name":"T18858","type":"text","text":"August, 1885\nBuffalo Bill's Wild West show came to town. Someone threw a playing card in the air and Annie Oakley shot it ten times.  What a show!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,443,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1330":{"name":"T188612","type":"text","text":"December, 1886\nThe snowstorms started early this year, and they sure are fierce. I think we're in for a long, cold winter.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,441,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1331":{"name":"T189012","type":"text","text":"December, 1890\nIn Wounded Knee, South Dakota, the U.S. Calvary killed about 200 Sioux Indians who had no weapons. Why did this tragedy happen?","align":0,"rect":[0,0,579,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1332":{"name":"T189412","type":"text","text":"December, 1894\nThe railroad strikes had me worried.  I thought I wouldn't be able to send my crops to the dealer. Luckily,  the strike was over by harvest time.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,414,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1333":{"name":"T189612","type":"text","text":"December, 1896\nThere's another gold rush. This time it's up in Canada, near the Klondike River.  Cousin George went up there, but we stayed here in Kansas.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,469,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1334":{"name":"T18988","type":"text","text":"August, 1898\nIn faraway Cuba, Teddy Roosevelt's Rough Riders charged up San Juan Hill.  We won Cuba from the Spanish, but we won't keep it.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,516,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1335":{"name":"T18974","type":"text","text":"April, 1897\nImmigrants from Russia brought a new kind of wheat to plant here.  It's called \"Turkey Red,\" and it grows well in dry soil like ours.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,451,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1336":{"name":"T190312","type":"text","text":"December, 1903\nThe Wright brothers went up in their flying machine in Kitty Hawk, North Carolina. The only flying machine in Kansas is a tractor in a tornado!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,463,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1337":{"name":"T190511","type":"text","text":"Novermber, 1905\nWe've put Teddy Roosevelt back in the White House. He understands the farmers in the Great Plains. He wants to help us find more water.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,455,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1338":{"name":"T19065","type":"text","text":"May, 1906\nCousin George was in San Francisco last  month for the big earthquake. He was so scared that he's moving back to Kansas!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,427,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1339":{"name":"T19084","type":"text","text":"April, 1908\nThe Ford Company put out a new car, the Model T. It's a good, solid car. Some folks are even using it to pull their plows!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,418,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1340":{"name":"T19098","type":"text","text":"August, 1909\nWe were glad when Congress passed the Enlarged Homestead Act, but most of our friends think that a 320-acre farm is still too small!","align":0,"rect":[0,0,516,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1341":{"name":"T19114","type":"text","text":"April, 1911\nThe F.W. Woolworth Company Inc. opened a \"5-and-dime\" store in town.  There are over 1,000 Woolworth stores across the country.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,410,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1342":{"name":"T19125","type":"text","text":"May, 1912\nLast month, the Titanic sank.  More than 1,000 people drowned, including a few millionaires. It just goes to show that money isn't everything.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,582,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1343":{"name":"T191311","type":"text","text":"November, 1913\nCongress passed the 16th Amendment. Now we have to pay income tax. I don't mind, as long as I don't have to fill out a lot of long forms.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,577,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1344":{"name":"T19164","type":"text","text":"April, 1916\nGermany has been threatening our ships. People say that we're about to enter the Great War.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,507,32],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1345":{"name":"T191812","type":"text","text":"December, 1918\nThe war is over, and Cousin George is coming home from France. He kept his head down during the shooting, but he's getting a medal.","align":0,"rect":[0,0,398,48],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1346":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,328,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1347":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,328,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1348":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,328,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1349":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,328,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"ascent":12,"style":0,"size":12,"color":"#000000","font":"Arial"}]},"1350":{"name":"","type":"text","text":"","align":0,"rect":[0,0,328,16],"styles":[{"start":0,"height":16,"